WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.435 line:0%
-I want to say
welcome back to the show

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:03.937 line:0%
because you actually made
your late-night debut

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:05.705 line:0%
on our show
with "Drivers License."

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.640 line:0%
-"Drivers License." Yep.
-But we never chatted.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:09.109 line:0%
-I know.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.543 line:0%
I'm such a fan of the show.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.946 line:0%
Growing up, I used to watch it
every night with my parents.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:15.148
I'm such a huge fan,
so it's an honor to be here.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:18.418
You actually -- I met you,
um, maybe three year--

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.486
You wouldn't have remembered.
It was -- It was so long ago.

00:00:20.486 --> 00:00:21.955
-What do you mean,
I wouldn't remember?

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.723
-It was in a group of people,
but there was a group of people,

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:25.158
and they were like,
"Hey, hey, hey."

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:27.393
And you actually went up to
my mom and you gave her a hug.

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.896
And it is her bragging rights
for the rest of her life.

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.497
She loves you so much.
-Oh, my gosh.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.966
-She sends her regards and she
says, "Thank you for the hug."

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:37.503
-Hi, Mom! Hi! Yeah.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:40.072
Uh, I follow you
on the socials, and I --

00:00:40.072 --> 00:00:42.308
You're a great follow,
by the way,

00:00:42.308 --> 00:00:44.877
if you like the social media.

00:00:44.877 --> 00:00:47.146
But I noticed that
you don't follow anyone back.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:48.715
-Oh. I'm sorry.

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.017
If I was following one person,
it'd be you, though, I hope.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.418
-Thank you. Oh, yeah.
Really, though...

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:55.421
-Ah, [bleep].
-Any reason why?

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:56.923
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:59.291
-No, you know,
I try to follow zero people

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:01.327
because it helps me
be off of my phone,

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.962
you know,
off of social media.

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:06.565
But I had this very embarrassing
encounter once

00:01:06.565 --> 00:01:09.235
where I was stalking my ex,
as one does.

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.137
Sue me. Sorry.

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:13.973
And, um --
And I accidentally followed him

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.642
because I was stalking him, and
I was just following one person,

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.411
so it was super obvious
that I was following him.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:20.947
And my friend ran into my room
and was like, "Oh, my God!

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.782
Did you mean to follow him?
Like, unfollow him!"

00:01:22.782 --> 00:01:24.183
And I went
and I grabbed my phone.

00:01:24.183 --> 00:01:25.552
I'm like,
"Oh, shoot! Oh, my God!"

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:27.052
And I went to open
the Instagram app.

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.389
And the second that I opened
the app, my phone died.

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.090
-Oh, my gosh!
-Couldn't find the charger.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:33.926
So I was just following
my ex for a while.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.628
-Did it come out
that you were --

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.331
Yeah, and people were like,
"Oh, my gosh! She's hacked!"

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:41.234
And I'm like, "Yeah, you guys.
Be safe." Like...

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:43.135
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.204
"Get your two-factor
authentication, you guys."

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:46.940
-You weren't hacked it all.
You did it yourself.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.641
-Yeah. Sorry.
-Oh, my gosh. Alright.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.843
So now -- But you don't make
that mistake again.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:52.578
-No, no. I have a Finsta now,
so I'm safe.

00:01:52.578 --> 00:01:54.180
-You have a Finsta.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.215
Do you have a Finsta, Jimmy.
-I need a Finsta.

00:01:56.215 --> 00:01:58.150
-Yeah. You need a Finsta.
-A fake Instagram.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.552
-Fake Instagram. Yeah.

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:01.087
So you can just lurk
and be curious.

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:02.989
-Yeah. And like things
and look at things and...

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.824
Wait. I'm totally getting
a Finsta this week.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.858
-Yeah. Okay.
-Alright. Thank you.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:07.326
I appreciate it.
I want to talk to you.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:08.894
I have so many things
to talk to you about.

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.997
First of all,
congratulations on "GUTS."

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.832
-Thank you.
-Uh, this is unbelievable.

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:14.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:17.403
Went right to number one
when it released.

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.906
And then you got nominated
just now for six Grammys.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.607
Uh...

00:02:21.607 --> 00:02:23.876
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.213
You have three Grammys on your
shelf already from "Sour,"

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.114
but how does it feel
to be nominated for six?

00:02:29.114 --> 00:02:31.184
I mean, you're part of this --
This is your year now.

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.252
-It's so surreal.
I actually can't believe it.

00:02:33.252 --> 00:02:34.921
I feel like
the luckiest girl alive.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:36.956
I used to go
to the Grammy Museum

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.958
all the time when I was younger,
and, actually,

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:41.293
my mom and I used to, like,
make ballots for the Grammys,

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.528
like, when the Grammys
were on TV.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:43.662
When I was like 12, I'd be like,

00:02:43.662 --> 00:02:45.264
"I think this album
is going to win."

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.032
And, like, we'd do --
place bets and stuff.

00:02:47.032 --> 00:02:48.568
-No way!
-So it's a super-big deal.

00:02:48.568 --> 00:02:49.802
Yeah, it's just --
it's such an honor

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.136
to be included in a group

00:02:51.136 --> 00:02:53.906
with all these artists
that I just am so inspired by.

00:02:53.906 --> 00:02:55.641
-You more than
hold your own, bud.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.977
And now here we go.
This "Hunger Games" soundtrack.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:01.447
The new song is called
"Can't Catch Me Now."

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:04.917
What's it like writing a song
for a movie or, like --

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.085
Because you're not --

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.887
This, you write
your songs for you.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.321
-Yeah, that's like my diary,

00:03:09.321 --> 00:03:11.724
but this was a totally
different experience for me

00:03:11.724 --> 00:03:13.159
as a songwriter.
It was so much fun.

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:15.928
I'm such a big fan
of all things "Hunger Games,"

00:03:15.928 --> 00:03:18.731
and I love the soundtracks,
and so when they asked

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:20.333
if I wanted to write it,
I was so stoked.

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.468
And I went in
and watched the movie

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.970
and was really inspired by
the main character, Lucy Gray.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.206
Um, and so it was super-fun
to get to write a song

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.509
